    "data": {
      "title": "Hungry Candy Wheel",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "candies = input()\nresult = \"\"\nwhile candies:\n    digit = candies[0]\n    result += digit\n    candies = candies[1:]\n    if candies:\n        turns = int(digit) % len(candies)\n        candies = candies[turns:] + candies[:turns]\nprint(result)\n",
      "statement": "The string [[candies]] represents a queue of candies, from first to last. Each digit represents one candy.\n\nRepeat these steps until the queue is empty:\n\n1. Eat and remove the <<first candy>>. This candy never returns to the queue. Record its digit for the output.\n2. Perform as many moves as the value of the digit just eaten. Each move takes the <<first remaining candy>> and places that candy at the <<end of the queue>>. Skip this step if the queue is empty.\n\nPrint the recorded digits as a single string, in the order the candies were eaten.\n\n<<Example:>>\nFor [[candies]] = {{24135}}:\n\nEat {{2}}. The remaining queue is {{4135}}.\n\nPerform {{2}} moves:\n- First move: place {{4}} at the end. The queue becomes {{1354}}.\n- Second move: place {{1}} at the end. The queue becomes {{3541}}.\n\nNext, eat {{3}}, then perform {{3}} moves on the remaining queue.\n\nContinue until all candies are eaten. The output is {{23514}}.",
